{
  "about": "Chart packs built from NOAA's Chart Display Service MBTiles (checked each month, built when NOAA's files change). Each area is west, south, east, north in degrees and the deepest zoom kept there: out to about 200 nm offshore light (zoom 10), the region out to 60-80 nm at 12 or 13, a band about 5 nm wide along the coast and the straits and sounds deeper, harbours deepest. Every pack starts at zoom 3, where NOAA's charts start, so they show however far out the map is zoomed. Zoom 10 shows about 40 km across a phone screen, 12 about 10 km, 14 about 2.5 km, 16 about 600 m. The VMR holds 8 packs at most. Each region is also built as a max-detail pack (<name>-max.vmrchart): every tile NOAA has inside the region's box at every zoom, nothing left out; add \"max\": false to a region to skip it. The VMR keeps one of a region's two.",
